<title>AUSTRALIA: Faulding forms new research division.</title>
<headline>Faulding forms new research division.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical group F.H. Faulding and Co Ltd said on Friday it had formed a new operating division, Faulding Soltec DDS, dedicated to developing and commercialising innovative drug delivery systems.</p>
<p>Faulding said the move built on synergies arising from the 1996 acquisition of Melbourne research and development company Soltec Research Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>Faulding chief executive Ed Tweddell said the creation of the new division added further scope to the company's mission of making medicines work better, meeting global trends.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
